      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose doesn't add meaningful pain relief.\n\nHere are some options that stay within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum, and is usually reserved for short-term use with food.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day, a more typical upper range.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, 3 or 4 times daily.** This is 1,200 to 1,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. If the pain needs more than an NSAID can safely give, you could add scheduled acetaminophen or consider another drug class.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you want a different regimen, send the details."
      }
